Source: gitcha
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: inputloop <nathanielfrankford@gmail.com>
# npm fetches the server's dependencies from the committed lockfile at build time (network, or a filled npm cache).
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), nodejs (>= 20), npm
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/inputloop/gitcha
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/inputloop/gitcha.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: inputloop-gitcha
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20), git, adduser
# ${gitcha:Recommends} is "cassandra" unless built with the pkg.gitcha.nocassandra profile.
Recommends: ${gitcha:Recommends}, gnupg, openssh-server, caddy
Description: Gitcha: forge, registry, hosting and community for inputloop
 Self-hosted packages, git repositories (HTTPS and SSH), static sites with
 custom domains, CI and lambda functions run by separate runners, billing with
 Stripe and PayPal, agents and Second Reader reviews, a social crawl, and
 operations tickets.  Every account uses a password and an authenticator app.
 .
 Its database lives in Apache Cassandra or in one file.  debconf asks for the
 settings, so a preseed file can install many servers unattended.  It starts
 only when that is asked for.

Package: inputloop-gitcha-runner
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20), adduser
Recommends: bcontain
Description: Gitcha runner: CI jobs and functions in bContain VMs
 Registers with a Gitcha server, takes jobs, runs each in its own throwaway
 bContain VM, streams the log back and reports the result.  debconf can take
 the server and a registration token, so a preseed file registers it
 unattended.  It starts only when that is asked for.
